    "explanation": "To both parties. The rider is right in substance and the fare is recomputed; the driver keeps the rest.\n\nESTABLISHMENT. The GPS trace (EV-GPS-02848, weight 1.0) is clean for policy purposes: 130 fixes at a 10-second sample interval, 100.0% coverage, zero gaps, max_gap_sec 0 s, so none of POL-RD-07(a)-(c) fires and the trace is not impaired. Its governing figure, gps_trace.trace_distance_km = 14.31 km, is measured against the booked optimal of 2.4 km carried on the trip record (EV-TRIP-02848, weight 1.0). Excess = 11.91 km, i.e. 496.25% of optimal. Both POL-RD-01 tests pass (over 20% of optimal and over 0.8 km absolute), so the deviation is ESTABLISHED, and it is additionally MATERIAL (over 50% and over 8.0 km). The rider's POL-RD-08(a) burden is discharged: trip_id TRP-02848 and the start/end timestamps match across trip record, trace and fare breakdown.\n\nTHE DRIVER'S EXPLANATION. \"The rider changed the destination verbally\" is a bare assertion citing no evidence ID and no clause. Under POL-RD-08 it carries no weight and is discarded: the chat log (EV-CHAT-02848, weight 1.0) contains zero messages, so there is no rider instruction meeting POL-RD-04(a)-(c), and no waypoint_hint or named road for the trace to be tested against; the trip record shows original_pickup, original_dropoff, pickup_amended_at and dropoff_amended_at all null, so POL-RD-05 has no amended endpoint and no amendment timestamp to run against. Nothing reduces the excess. No traffic advisory covers this trip either: EV-ADVIS-02848-01 is MISSING, weight 0.0, issue MISSING_ARTIFACT, so POL-RD-03 cannot be run and any external-traffic explanation is weightless under POL-RD-08 (POL-RD-13; the missing advisory no party properly cited is a gap in the bundle, not a POL-RD-10(5) contradiction). No POL-RD-10 trigger fires: the trace is un-impaired, identifiers and timestamps agree, and the refund is far below SGD 150.00.\n\nREMEDY (POL-RD-02, fare model METERED and quoted_fare_sgd null, so POL-RD-11 does not close the distance-and-time route; the surge multiplier is read from fare_breakdown.surge_multiplier = 1.0, the only artifact that carries it):\n  charged_total (EV-FARE-02848) = 21.35\n  recomputed_fare = (3.80 + 0.75 x 2.4 + 0.28 x 5.0) x 1.0 + 0.80 platform fee + 0 ERP/tolls = 7.80\n  refund = 21.35 - 7.80 = 13.55\nThe refund is 63.47% of charged_total - above the SGD 0.50 de minimis and below the 90% full-refund share - so the outcome is PARTIAL_REFUND of SGD 13.55, which is already a multiple of SGD 0.05.\n\nPASS-THROUGH AND PATTERN. The fare breakdown carries no ERP gantry, no tolls and no airport surcharge on a trip that neither originates nor ends at an airport, so POL-RD-09 adds nothing on top of 13.55 and there is no billing-integrity referral. The POL-RD-06 pattern test is not met (deviation_flags_90d 0 over completed_trips_90d 210), so there is no FULL_REFUND uplift and no driver-conduct referral. No driver compensation arises: the billed 14.3 km is not short of the trace's 14.31 km by more than 1.0 km. The reference-only profile fields the advocates mentioned were not used as a ground of decision.\n\nConfidence is 0.9, within the cap of 1.0 set by the weight of the artifacts carrying the deciding facts (trip record, GPS trace and fare breakdown, all weight 1.0). The monetary effect of SGD 13.55 exceeds the POL-GEN-05 execution threshold of SGD 8.00, so the ruling issues but the amount is held for release rather than executed automatically. This is a provisional ruling; either party may appeal under POL-GEN-04."
